WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.258
I came to New York
with a travel toothbrush.

00:10.219 --> 00:13.013
It's one of those cheap ones
with a little plastic cap on top.

00:13.805 --> 00:17.434
Back then, I would, uh, couch surf,
mostly with hookups,

00:17.976 --> 00:22.147
sometimes with older women
who enjoyed watching me bathe their dogs.

00:22.731 --> 00:24.274
Got scratched up real bad back then.

00:25.692 --> 00:27.778
But a few months ago,
I found myself here in Queens.

00:28.987 --> 00:31.531
And I, uh, found a place to call home.

00:32.699 --> 00:36.286
And I found a bed with Transformers sheets
that I share with another adult man.

00:37.496 --> 00:40.040
You know, just last week,
I finally got a new toothbrush.

00:41.500 --> 00:44.211
It's electric. Came with a little stand.
Plugs into the wall. It's real nice.

00:44.294 --> 00:45.379
Reaches all the way back.

00:49.007 --> 00:50.342
But I still keep this one,

00:52.010 --> 00:53.887
just to remind myself of a time

00:54.763 --> 00:56.139
when I was a stranger here.

00:57.140 --> 01:01.645
So that's why I'm running for
president of the homeowners association.

01:02.437 --> 01:05.941
To make us all feel
just a little less like strangers.

01:06.525 --> 01:10.195
To make us all feel a little more at home.

01:11.363 --> 01:12.614
- Thank you.
- Whoo!

01:12.698 --> 01:14.533
- We love you!
- Yeah!

01:16.118 --> 01:17.411
We love you!

01:17.494 --> 01:19.871
- I share a bed with that man. We spoon.
- That's the guy.

01:19.955 --> 01:22.583
Mr. Baker,
the question was about potholes.

01:23.166 --> 01:24.459
Yes.

01:24.543 --> 01:25.919
I'm against them.

01:26.712 --> 01:27.879
Whoo!

01:27.963 --> 01:29.590
Give Donna a cognition test!

01:31.466 --> 01:33.468
- Ma'am.
- We were all thinking it.

01:34.094 --> 01:39.349
Next up, we have our incumbent,
HOA president, Sandy Adler.

01:39.433 --> 01:43.145
- Thank you, Doreen. Thank you all.
- Go, Daddy!

01:43.228 --> 01:48.442
First of all, I just wanna say that
I was very moved by the toothbrush thing.

01:48.525 --> 01:51.695
- Thank you.
- I usually carry floss picks with me,

01:51.778 --> 01:56.199
but my daughter Nina told me
not to pick a fight tonight.

01:56.283 --> 01:58.618
Sandy.

01:59.286 --> 02:00.495
And I you won't. And I won't.

02:00.579 --> 02:01.580
Fuck, he's really good.

02:01.663 --> 02:04.666
I know. 17 straight terms.
Polls have him up by four points.

02:06.501 --> 02:08.587
- There are polls for this? Mmm.
- Yeah, I made them. Yeah. Yeah.

02:08.670 --> 02:10.464
Donna, you're up next.

02:11.965 --> 02:17.846
There's a squirrel in my house
that brings me Turkish delights.

02:20.515 --> 02:22.017
- Cognition test!
- Issa.

02:26.396 --> 02:27.939
♪ I need some bad advice ♪

02:33.028 --> 02:34.696
♪ Stay up tonight ♪

02:35.697 --> 02:36.823
♪ We'll make it out alive ♪

02:39.451 --> 02:41.286
I'm telling you,
he doesn't even kill ants.

02:41.370 --> 02:43.580
Thank you so much again for helping me...

02:46.500 --> 02:47.501
What?

02:47.584 --> 02:48.919
I thought you spoke Spanish.

02:49.002 --> 02:51.213
Yeah, I mean, he's genuinely kind, Sharon.

02:51.296 --> 02:54.591
He's like Mr. Rogers,
if Mr. Rogers had figured out his hair.

02:54.675 --> 02:56.551
- Aw, you mean that?
- Go away.

02:56.635 --> 02:58.136
You can't hear me say nice things.

02:58.220 --> 03:00.555
- Okay. Guys?
- Ooh. Can you hold?

03:00.639 --> 03:02.683
Okay, take a look at this map.
There are 83 votes up for grabs today,

03:02.766 --> 03:05.268
and we're taking a shot
at every single goddamn one.

03:05.352 --> 03:07.479
- This is a two-man race now.
- Ugh, poor Donna.

03:07.562 --> 03:10.107
- She drove straight through that Carvel.
- Oh, no, she's fine.

03:10.190 --> 03:12.359
- Uh, where's Samir?
- Mentally or physically?

03:12.442 --> 03:15.195
- Mentally, in deep denial.
- Hmm.

03:15.278 --> 03:16.863
- Physically, in his bedroom.
- Mm-hmm.

03:16.947 --> 03:18.448
- Sharon, I'm back.
- Oh.

03:18.532 --> 03:20.158
Lisa?
Oh, sorry. Lisa?

03:20.242 --> 03:21.284
Samy, I'm just worried.

03:21.368 --> 03:24.329
Carly, baby,
I promise you it's gonna be fine.

03:24.413 --> 03:27.290
Look, we can FaceTime. We can Zoom.

03:27.374 --> 03:28.792
All distance is the same now.

03:28.875 --> 03:32.796
Ugh. How did I match to Seattle?
It was so deep on my rank list.

03:32.879 --> 03:34.548
Let's not do that. Let's think positive.

03:34.631 --> 03:37.217
Dental residency is insanely competitive.

03:37.300 --> 03:39.803
Plus, Seattle is an amazing city, right?

03:39.886 --> 03:42.681
Good seafood. Great-Great needles.

03:42.764 --> 03:45.892
It's so frustrating. I had my entire life
planned out in New York,

03:45.976 --> 03:47.394
and now I don't know what I'm gonna...

03:47.477 --> 03:48.937
Carly. Oh.

03:49.771 --> 03:50.856
Baby, you're cutting out.

03:51.440 --> 03:53.358
It said my connection was unstable.

03:53.442 --> 03:56.111
Aw! That's why we practice, though, right?
That's why we practice.

03:56.194 --> 03:58.655
Samir, how are we supposed to make it
through a full year of this?

03:58.738 --> 04:00.407
Hey, do I look worried?

04:01.116 --> 04:02.242
We got this, okay?

04:02.325 --> 04:04.744
Also, look,
I added Seattle to my weather app.

04:04.828 --> 04:06.538
That way when it rains for you,
it rains for me.

04:07.164 --> 04:08.540
Baby, that's Seattle, Texas.

04:09.207 --> 04:10.417
There's a Seattle, Texas?

04:10.500 --> 04:12.210
Are you sure you didn't match there?

04:13.920 --> 04:15.630
And that's what I thought. Yep.

04:15.714 --> 04:17.466
Okay, we can expect your vote? Oh!

04:17.549 --> 04:20.135
- Janice, you're an angel!
- Okay, guys, how's it going?

04:20.218 --> 04:21.344
- Paul Baker?
- Yeah.

04:21.428 --> 04:24.014
Patty from Elm Street is being such
an asshole about drainage.

04:24.097 --> 04:25.182
- I can't.
- Fair.

04:25.265 --> 04:26.475
- Okay, let me handle. Yeah.
- Take her.

04:26.558 --> 04:28.727
Hey, Jules, thank you again
for helping out. I really appreciate it.

04:29.311 --> 04:30.479
I'm just so proud of you

04:30.562 --> 04:32.272
- for getting involved.
- Mmm.

04:32.355 --> 04:35.650
Do you know I once organized an entire
front row at a Marc Jacobs show?

04:35.734 --> 04:37.027
- Oh, really? For what cause?
- Mm-hmm.

04:37.652 --> 04:39.196
- Just to get dinner after.
- Oh.

04:39.279 --> 04:41.114
Guys, the coverage is starting.

04:41.198 --> 04:42.532
- Oh.
- Carly. Samir.

04:42.616 --> 04:44.951
- Oh, my God. Okay.
- Coming!

04:45.035 --> 04:48.205
Hello, everyone who lives east of
Forest Avenue and west of Franklin Road.

04:48.288 --> 04:50.791
I'm Katie Yeoh,
senior at Garfield High School

04:50.874 --> 04:52.793
and president of the journalism club.

04:52.876 --> 04:54.836
- I founded that club. Do you know that?
- Yes.

04:54.920 --> 04:57.297
- Shh.
- I'm covering the HOA election today

04:57.380 --> 04:59.382
because that is the assignment
Mr. De la Croix gave me.

04:59.466 --> 05:01.426
Okay. Well, that's a good beat, Katie.
Be grateful.

05:01.510 --> 05:03.011
...excitement in the air, we're hoping for...

05:03.094 --> 05:04.095
You guys good?

05:04.179 --> 05:07.974
- And I'll be here to cover it all...
- Hmm? Yes. We are great.

05:08.558 --> 05:10.143
- Yeah.
- Great.

05:10.894 --> 05:13.396
Polls have been open
for just under an hour, and so far,

05:13.480 --> 05:16.900
incumbent Sandy Adler has eight marbles
to Paul Baker's six.

05:16.983 --> 05:18.276
Okay, okay.

05:18.360 --> 05:19.694
Oh, my God! Okay!

05:19.778 --> 05:22.280
- Yes, yes, yes!
- We're in this thing, people.

05:22.364 --> 05:24.241
Okay, uh, let's keep the phone lines hot.

05:24.324 --> 05:25.951
Yes, yes, yes. Okay.

05:26.034 --> 05:27.369
I'll get that. Okay.

05:28.578 --> 05:29.788
- Hi.
- Wow.

05:29.871 --> 05:31.581
- Hi.
- Hi.

05:31.665 --> 05:33.583
- Come in.
- Oh. Thank you.

05:33.667 --> 05:35.085
- Thank you.
- Paul Baker.

05:35.168 --> 05:37.003
- Oh, Sandy, what are you doing here?
- Hey.

05:37.087 --> 05:38.839
- Oh, we just stopped by to wish you luck.
- Aw.

05:38.922 --> 05:42.467
- You're a good kid, you know? Yeah.
- Class all the way with this guy, huh?

05:42.551 --> 05:44.845
Truly, I-I walk in the...
in the footsteps of giants.

05:44.928 --> 05:46.388
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey, real quick,

05:46.471 --> 05:48.098
is there a restroom I could use?

05:48.181 --> 05:50.392
You get to be my age,
it's, like, every five minutes.

05:50.475 --> 05:51.643
- Yeah. Okay.
- Doctor says

05:51.726 --> 05:54.688
it's not a prostate thing or anything,
but, you know, then what is it?

05:54.771 --> 05:55.856
That's what I wanna know.

05:55.939 --> 05:57.315
- Oh, I'm, uh, Billie Schaeffer...
- Hi.

05:57.399 --> 05:58.692
...by the way,
Paul Baker's campaign manager.

05:58.775 --> 06:00.569
Nina Adler, Sandy's daughter.

06:00.652 --> 06:02.070
Your dad seems so sweet.

06:02.153 --> 06:04.364
- Oh, I know. He's the best.
- Aw.

06:04.447 --> 06:06.283
Yeah, he means the world to me, and...

06:07.200 --> 06:09.369
and, you know,
the HOA means the world to him.

06:09.953 --> 06:13.081
Oh, my God,
you're standing so close to me.

06:13.164 --> 06:15.667
- Oh, yeah. I'm intimidating you.
- What?

06:15.750 --> 06:17.961
Here's the thing about 70-year-old men,

06:18.628 --> 06:21.256
Billie Schaeffer, they're bored as fuck.

06:21.339 --> 06:22.507
They're retired.

06:22.591 --> 06:25.218
Their wives want them out of the house,
so they find a little hobby.

06:25.302 --> 06:29.306
And for my dad, he found the HOA.
Now, you probably don't get this,

06:29.389 --> 06:32.309
but when you stop working,
you can get a little lost.

06:32.392 --> 06:33.560
I actually do understand that.

06:33.643 --> 06:36.521
The HOA is not for you.

06:36.605 --> 06:38.064
Do you understand?

06:38.607 --> 06:40.692
Do you all live here, huh?
All five of you?

06:41.276 --> 06:42.277
Yes.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.905
You know, three or more unrelated adults
living under the same roof

06:44.988 --> 06:47.782
is what the city of Queens
likes to call a zoning violation.

06:47.866 --> 06:52.579
It's just a little tidbit
I picked up from the HOA.

06:53.496 --> 06:54.497
Okay.

06:54.998 --> 06:58.168
I mean, this is the time of your life
when your friends are your family.

06:58.251 --> 06:59.461
Oh, my God, that's so cute.

07:00.337 --> 07:03.006
Like, you think you're the first people
to be young and adorable in New York?

07:03.089 --> 07:05.091
Don't answer that. Not so.

07:05.175 --> 07:06.509
So guess what?

07:06.593 --> 07:11.139
If your friend unseats my dad today, this
little sex dungeon that you all reside in...

07:11.222 --> 07:13.183
...I'm gonna report it.

07:14.017 --> 07:15.727
And then I'm gonna blow it to pieces.

07:16.645 --> 07:18.438
- When it comes to recycling...
- You ready, Daddy?

07:18.521 --> 07:20.106
- Yeah. Yeah, Nin, yeah.
- Yeah?

07:20.857 --> 07:22.817
- Did you get it all out?
- Well, most of it.

07:22.901 --> 07:25.654
- Okay, great.
- Well, happy election day, gang.

07:25.737 --> 07:27.280
- Happy election day.
- Good luck, guys.

07:27.364 --> 07:30.283
- May the best man win, you know?
- Good luck. All right.

07:30.367 --> 07:32.077
- Bye. Okay.
- Come on, Nin.

07:32.160 --> 07:33.495
Okay, bye, guys.

07:33.578 --> 07:35.205
Take care. Drive safe.

07:36.247 --> 07:38.166
He peed so much.

07:39.376 --> 07:41.378
So many different directions.

07:43.046 --> 07:44.047
What?

07:47.967 --> 07:49.469
It's not fair. This is our home.

07:49.552 --> 07:51.012
It's fucking blackmail.

07:51.096 --> 07:53.556
No, it's politics.
I mean, she's House of Cards'ing us.

07:53.640 --> 07:54.683
She touched you?

07:54.766 --> 07:55.892
- What?
- What?

07:55.975 --> 07:57.644
Okay, that's it, right? I-I-I'll just...

07:57.727 --> 07:59.562
I will drop out,
and everything will be fine.

07:59.646 --> 08:01.356
No, you can't drop out
once voting started,

08:01.439 --> 08:03.191
and we're already 30 marbles deep.

08:03.274 --> 08:04.693
Fuck. Ugh, dude.

08:04.776 --> 08:06.194
Oh, this is all my fault, man.

08:06.277 --> 08:10.031
I was just trying to lay roots,
but I guess instead

08:10.115 --> 08:12.784
I'm like one of those roots
that cracked the sidewalk.

08:12.867 --> 08:14.536
So, I'm so sorry, guys.

08:14.619 --> 08:16.329
- You didn't know. Yeah.
- No, no.

08:16.413 --> 08:18.331
- Guys, new results are in.
- Oh, my God.

08:18.415 --> 08:19.874
Well,

08:19.958 --> 08:21.418
we've got an exciting race update.

08:21.501 --> 08:23.461
Newcomer Paul Baker has taken the lead...

08:23.545 --> 08:25.547
- No.
- ...with 21 marbles to Adler's 19.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.465
- Oh, shit.
- Oh, my God, this is it.

08:27.549 --> 08:29.050
We're gonna have to move out.

08:32.011 --> 08:33.179
No.

08:33.263 --> 08:34.556
- We're not.
- What?

08:35.140 --> 08:37.225
If there's one thing I know,
it's how not to get a job.

08:38.101 --> 08:42.105
It's just a question
of manpower and targeting.

08:42.188 --> 08:44.774
- This is Kerry, Iowa, 2004.
- What is that? Is that a shooting?

08:44.858 --> 08:46.192
No.

08:46.276 --> 08:47.819
- Right?
- No.

08:48.486 --> 08:49.904
Okay. No.

08:49.988 --> 08:51.990
Wait, I-I'm sorry, Bills.
W-What are you saying?

08:52.073 --> 08:53.992
I'm saying we're gonna tank this campaign.

08:54.075 --> 08:55.744
Samir and Carly, man the phones.

08:55.827 --> 08:57.996
Issa and Anton, we need boots
on the ground at the library.

08:58.079 --> 09:01.583
Julia Fox, you are famous, and I
don't feel comfortable bossing you around.

09:01.666 --> 09:02.667
That's fair.

09:02.751 --> 09:04.753
Okay, people, this is no longer
a campaign for Paul Baker.

09:04.836 --> 09:06.129
This is a campaign against him.

09:06.212 --> 09:09.758
We are going to lose this election
and keep our house. Giddyap.

09:11.176 --> 09:12.594
How do you feel about "giddyap"?

09:12.677 --> 09:14.345
Not great. Let me run that back.

09:14.429 --> 09:15.847
- Okay.
- Um...

09:15.930 --> 09:17.474
- Let's go!
- There we go.

09:17.557 --> 09:19.434
- Yes! Let's lose this!
- Yeah.

09:25.398 --> 09:28.026
This is crazy. I always thought we were
gonna live in that house forever.

09:28.109 --> 09:30.695
And it'd be so cute, and I'd get sad,

09:30.779 --> 09:33.198
and then I would move out and try
to spin off, and that wouldn't work,

09:33.281 --> 09:34.908
so I'd move back in,
and it would get cute again.

09:36.534 --> 09:37.869
- David, David. David.
- Oh. Oh.

09:37.952 --> 09:40.205
- Hi, David. I love this vest.
- Hi.

09:40.288 --> 09:42.123
Um, did you decide
who you're voting for today?

09:42.207 --> 09:44.876
I did. Our phone call
last week convinced me.

09:44.959 --> 09:48.129
Okay. Okay, David, David, I wonder
if you've been convinced too quickly.

09:48.213 --> 09:49.839
- Yeah.
- Right? You have a tendency to do that.

09:49.923 --> 09:51.341
- Ugh.
- Remember the time-share?

09:51.424 --> 09:52.425
- What?
- David.

09:52.509 --> 09:55.220
You said that Paul Baker
was like home to you.

09:55.303 --> 09:58.056
- What?
- No, no, I don't... No.

09:58.139 --> 09:59.682
Yeah, you said you never recycle,

09:59.766 --> 10:02.477
but you do it now to impress him,
even when he's not there.

10:03.353 --> 10:04.395
You said that?

10:04.938 --> 10:06.689
- Hmm? I...
- Oh, excuse me.

10:06.773 --> 10:09.484
- Hi. What are you doing?
- Oh, shit. It's the librarian. Charm her.

10:09.567 --> 10:11.444
- Charm her.
- You can't talk to the voters.

10:11.528 --> 10:12.570
Oh. Um, hi.

10:12.654 --> 10:14.239
- Hi.
- Are-Are-Are you the librarian here?

10:14.322 --> 10:15.907
- Yes.
- Thank you for your service.

10:15.990 --> 10:18.993
Look at your name.
Margaux, like Château.

10:19.077 --> 10:20.912
Or "Mar-gocks,"
like no name we've ever heard.

10:21.538 --> 10:25.250
Okay. Well, you guys seem great.

10:25.333 --> 10:26.376
- Oh, thank you.
- Thank you.

10:26.459 --> 10:27.669
But, um...

10:27.752 --> 10:29.921
You'll have
to head out now, lassies.

10:32.382 --> 10:33.424
- Sorry?
- What?

10:33.508 --> 10:34.968
Um, sorry, just Irish.

10:35.510 --> 10:40.056
I felt weird about asking you guys
to leave, so I was doing Irish.

10:41.683 --> 10:43.434
Oh, my God,
she's a weird little guy.

10:45.186 --> 10:46.729
Wow. So, do you work here then?

10:46.813 --> 10:49.482
Is this your here salt mine,
where you're burning your midnight oil?

10:49.566 --> 10:51.651
Me, if I was on a black-and-white photo.

10:51.734 --> 10:55.572
Well, you know, this here
is my saloon, if you will and please.

10:55.655 --> 10:57.907
Well,
then you better pour me a whiskey

10:57.991 --> 11:00.493
and call me your mayor because
I wanna get to know this place.

11:02.120 --> 11:03.788
Go. Voter intimidate. Go.

11:03.872 --> 11:05.874
David, David,
Paul Baker had a gun to my head

11:05.957 --> 11:07.333
as I said those things, so...

11:08.626 --> 11:09.794
- What?
- Yes.

11:10.378 --> 11:12.589
Things are heating up
at the Bayside North Library,

11:12.672 --> 11:14.549
and we are covering it all.

11:14.632 --> 11:16.009
So you're doing long distance.

11:16.092 --> 11:17.385
- Yeah.
- That's great.

11:17.468 --> 11:19.012
- Yeah.
- Okay.

11:19.637 --> 11:22.640
Thank you, Julia Fox,
'cause some people were saying...

11:22.724 --> 11:24.767
Carly, Julia Fox said we're gonna be fine.

11:24.851 --> 11:26.060
Oh. She's on the phone.

11:26.144 --> 11:28.563
No, I mean you're gonna break up, but...

11:29.898 --> 11:32.025
- What? No. Why?
- That's how long distance works.

11:32.108 --> 11:34.485
You give it your all
for the first three to four months,

11:34.569 --> 11:36.362
and eventually your relationship
will dwindle down

11:36.446 --> 11:38.072
to sending each other Instagram memes.

11:38.156 --> 11:41.409
You know, and there's chatbots for that.
So, what's the point?

11:41.492 --> 11:43.536
But that's not always how it goes,
though, right?

11:43.620 --> 11:48.082
Well, I-I mean, not-not always.
Like, Paris, London, that works.

11:48.666 --> 11:51.252
Even Paris, Lisbon, kinda works.

11:51.336 --> 11:52.545
Paris, Barcelona...

11:53.463 --> 11:55.215
Come on, I don't need to tell you.

11:56.966 --> 11:59.677
- Bills, where have you been?
- Yeah. No, no, I know, I know.

11:59.761 --> 12:01.554
I'm up, like, six marbles.
I-It's a disaster. I'm gonna win.

12:01.638 --> 12:03.264
Hey, it's okay. I'm on it, okay?

12:03.348 --> 12:05.141
- I called in backup.
- What backup?

12:05.225 --> 12:09.812
Well, if you wanna lose this election, we
need people who make you look unelectable.

12:11.189 --> 12:12.440
- You didn't.
- I did.

12:12.523 --> 12:14.400
- Billie.
- Baker!

12:14.484 --> 12:16.236
Let's fuck shit up!

12:26.663 --> 12:27.789
Samir, I have to go.

12:27.872 --> 12:29.457
- No. Julia.
- Yeah, I have to go. I'm sorry.

12:29.540 --> 12:31.751
- I'm really turned on by them.
- Julia, no.

12:31.834 --> 12:34.295
No, this is exactly my type.
I know. I'm sick. I'm sick. I have to go.

12:34.379 --> 12:35.713
- I'm sorry!
